{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":57,"description":"The provider correctly exposes setContent via useState, but nothing in the codebase registers a Contentstack Stack.livePreview callback to actually call setContent. The prescribed fix states: 'The livePreview callback (registered via Stack.livePreview from the Contentstack SDK at _app.tsx or equivalent bootstrap) then calls setContent with the updated content object.' Grep for livePreview/live_preview/includeDraft across src/ and pages/ returned zero results. Without this registration, setContent is never invoked, the context never updates reactively, and all acceptance criteria related to live preview displaying draft content and reflecting real-time edits are unmet.","suggestedFix":"Register Stack.livePreview at app bootstrap (e.g., in _app.tsx or a Contentstack initialization module). The callback should receive the updated content entry from the SDK and call setContent with the merged/updated IContentstackContent object. Example: Stack.livePreview({ live_preview: true, onEntryChange: (entry) => { setContent(prev => ({ ...prev, ...entry })); } }). Without this wiring, the reactive provider is dead code."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":0,"description":"No vitest unit tests were added for this change. The diff only modifies src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx with zero corresponding test files. Per review criteria, new features must have corresponding vitest unit tests in test/unit/ mirroring the src/ path. There are no tests verifying that setContent updates the context value and triggers re-renders of consumers, or that the initial state matches defaultContent.","suggestedFix":"Add test/unit/context/ContentstackContext.test.tsx with tests that: (1) verify initial content equals defaultContent, (2) verify calling setContent updates the context and consumers re-render with new content, (3) verify the context throws when used outside ContentstackProvider."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack/","line":0,"description":"The includeDraft flag is not propagated through the public-facing contentstack service functions (getEntry, getSingleEntry, getSingletonEntry). Per learned review rules and the root cause analysis, draft content will never be served because no caller passes includeDraft: true to the factory. Without this, activating preview mode cannot display draft CMS content — the first acceptance criterion is unmet. The provider change alone cannot fetch draft content; the query layer must support includeDraft.","suggestedFix":"Add includeDraft to the IContentstackGetEntry, IContentstackGetSingleEntry, and IContentstackGetSingletonEntry interfaces. Propagate includeDraft through getEntry/getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry to the ContentstackFactory. In the factory, when includeDraft is true, call addParam('include_draft', 'true') on the query. Then in getStaticProps (or equivalent page-level data fetching), read context.preview and pass includeDraft: true when preview mode is active."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":8,"description":"The IContentstackContent interface still uses untyped [any] for header, footer, page, and globalDictionary fields. While this is pre-existing, the diff touches this file and TypeScript strict compliance requires no untyped any without an explanatory comment.","suggestedFix":"Replace [any] with properly typed arrays (e.g., IHeader[], IFooter[], etc.) or add an explanatory comment for each any usage: // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any — type pending definition."}],"summary":"The ContentstackContext.tsx change correctly implements the first half of the prescribed minimal fix (useState + setContent in context value), matching the root cause analysis. However, the change is incomplete in three blocker-level ways: (1) No Stack.livePreview callback is registered anywhere in the codebase to actually call setContent — the reactive provider is dead code without this wiring; (2) No vitest unit tests were added; (3) The includeDraft flag is not propagated through the contentstack service layer, so draft content can never be fetched even if preview mode is active. All ten acceptance criteria are unmet because the live preview pipeline is broken at both the SDK callback registration layer and the query parameter layer. The fix must be completed by registering the livePreview callback, propagating includeDraft through the service functions, and adding unit tests."}
